{"availability":"available","full":"ykangw/VeriExCiting","name":"VeriExCiting","description":"Verify Existing Citations: detect AI-generated fake citations in academic papers","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":32,"forks":11,"created":"2025-02-07T20:47:13Z","updated":"2026-08-01T18:57:36Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://veriexcite.streamlit.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://veriexcite.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.226Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.226Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.226Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.226Z","stars":32,"forks":11}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["VeriExCite is a Python tool designed to help you verify the existence of citations in academic papers (PDF format). It extracts the bibliography section from a PDF, parses individual references, and then checks their validity against Crossref, Google Scholar, Arxiv, and Google Search.","The rise of powerful Large Language Models (LLMs) has brought with it the potential for generating realistic-looking, yet entirely fabricated, academic references. While tools like ZeroGPT attempt to detect LLM-generated text, they rely on \"black box\" deep learning methods, which are prone to both false positives and false negatives, making them unreliable for definitive judgments. However, the presence of fabricated references within a manuscript provides concrete evidence that (at least part) of the text may be LLM-generated. VeriExCite focuses on this crucial aspect of academic integrity.…","This flowchart illustrates the VeriExCite process:"],"features":["Extraction: Extracts the bibliography section from PDF documents.","Parsing: Uses Google Gemini API to parse references into structured data (title, authors, DOI, type, etc.)","Checks academic references against OpenAlex, Crossref, Google Scholar, and Arxiv.","Checks website references using their URL and Google Search.","Identifies potentially fabricated citations."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ykangw/VeriExCiting/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"da1044b497be86556083815a4a051175362c93430883f4dce78382c0c337349d","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.336Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.336Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"VeriExCite is a Python tool designed to help you verify the existence of citations in academic papers (PDF format). It extracts the bibliography section from a PDF, parses individual references, and then checks their validity against Crossref, Google Scholar, Arxiv, and Google Search.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ykangw/VeriExCiting/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"da1044b497be86556083815a4a051175362c93430883f4dce78382c0c337349d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ykangw/VeriExCiting/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.336Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-01T18:57:36Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ykangw/VeriExCiting/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:58.336Z","hash":"da1044b497be86556083815a4a051175362c93430883f4dce78382c0c337349d","originalBytes":7901,"storedBytes":7901,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["google","api","key","veriexcite","gemini","references","pdf","streamlit","app","set","warning","folder","python","reference","doi","list","match","model","path","search","academic","bibliography","count","crossref","explanations","fabricated","invalid","openalex","optional","print","recommended","web","each","explanation","found","one","pip","process","provided","run","scholar","section","text","title","tool","verified","author","bash","checks","does","file","free","install","models","parse","potentially","provides","quota","references.","results","secrets.toml","see","status","using","validated","verification","when","academics","against","any","api.","arx